//! Packages reached by a compilation's module imports, and metadata-only pin operations.
//!
//! Each manifest declares the available path, git, and archive pins. `load` retains the root's
//! declarations; `require` fetches and validates one alias when import discovery reaches it.
//! Validation enforces package identity, source boundaries, exports, and acyclic imports.
//! Unused dependencies contribute neither source nor build plans to a compilation.
//!
//! Explicit `fetch` visits the declared pins for offline work. `requireAll` checks the complete
//! local metadata graph for dependency editing. Neither evaluates package code.
//!
//! A `silk.local.toml` beside the root manifest, or else beside its workspace's root manifest,
//! names local checkouts in its `[overrides]` table (PACKAGE-009). Every dependency on an
//! overridden package, anywhere in the graph and whatever its source, reads that checkout instead,
//! and nothing is fetched for it.

